  {
   "key": "0x80..0x9F",
   "name": "bits 7-5 = 100",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "804-813"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
     "lines": "911-915"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Enter hunt mode is a command instruction bit; its legend notes that it has no effect in asynchronous mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "911-915",
       "sha": "ded25f2b0f3afc5f20f80e80f6f9b52f996224d0ec969e9ac2c992111b95cb35"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Enter hunt mode: 1 enables the search for SYNC characters; it has no effect in asynchronous mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "911-915",
       "sha": "ded25f2b0f3afc5f20f80e80f6f9b52f996224d0ec969e9ac2c992111b95cb35"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The CPU can command the receiver to enter the HUNT mode if synchronization is lost.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "804-805",
       "sha": "140541aa416125aad336e38a4ef100d321bdb8f84707bb42dd0922af3d4ea6b1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Entering hunt also sets all the used character bits in the buffer to one, preventing a false SYNDET from data left in the receive buffer.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "805-809",
       "sha": "2e75b992af7555d01cb40af5bfde0ccb802908b06a68405ca398f3709e93e85f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The SYNDET flip-flop is reset at each status read, whether internal or external SYNC is programmed; this does not make the 8251A return to HUNT.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:8251A.raw.txt",
       "lines": "809-813",
       "sha": "2b2d7d89108bcd5249082e3a0ca984aae4703e51f1202ed94fe48d5e3fdf0d0f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "106",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "absent",
     "row": "4",
     "text": "Entering hunt does not set the used receive buffer bits to one: the branch taken with hunt on only clears m_ext_syn_set and does not touch the buffer.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8251.cpp",
       "lines": "584-585",
       "sha": "6eac7c1a96c1d3c990c48fc08911e3af4f30ad151adfd8df0e97d4088b53d427"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "107",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "With hunt on, a command write also clears m_ext_syn_set.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8251.cpp",
       "lines": "584-585",
       "sha": "6eac7c1a96c1d3c990c48fc08911e3af4f30ad151adfd8df0e97d4088b53d427"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "108",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "A command write calls update_syndet(false) before the hunt bit is tested.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/i8251.cpp",
       "lines": "581",
       "sha": "a78446f46f4fe9b9ea11ba9ac6d5d97d687852c01c408a3ff805da8263767511"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
